+      "## Semantic speech\n\n````python\n```python\nfrom readio.api import Readio,\
+      \ SpeakRequest\n\nservice = Readio()\nrequest = SpeakRequest(text=\"Hello from\
+      \ Readio.\", voice=\"kokoro:v1.0/af_heart\")\nresult = service.synthesize(request)\n\
+      wav_bytes = result.audio.to_wav_bytes()\nprint(\n    result.audio.sample_rate,\n\
+      \    result.audio.channels,\n    result.audio.frames,\n    result.duration_seconds,\n\
+      )\n````\n\n`Readio.synthesize()` returns a `SpeakResult` containing an `AudioBuffer`.\
+      \ It does not play audio, write files, or persist workflow artifacts. Use `result.audio.write_wav(path)`\
+      \ when a WAV file is explicitly needed. `Readio.speak(request, play=True)` delegates\
+      \ to synthesis and optionally plays the result; the module-level `readio.api.speak(...)`\
+      \ remains available for compatibility.\n\nPass a `CancellationToken` to `synthesize()`\
+      \ when the application needs cooperative cancellation. Readio checks the token\
+      \ at stage boundaries. It does not interrupt a VoiceRender engine call already\
+      \ in progress."
