+      "## Application catalog and errors\n\nUse the `Readio` instance methods for\
+      \ normalized application catalog records. They return Readio-owned DTOs rather\
+      \ than VoiceRender descriptor objects:\n\n```python\nengines = service.list_engines()\n\
+      targets = service.list_targets(engines[0].id, language=\"en-US\", offline=True)\n\
+      voices = service.list_voices(\n    engine=engines[0].id,\n    target=targets[0].id,\n\
+      \    language=\"en-US\",\n    offline=True,\n)\noptions = service.list_engine_options(engines[0].id,\
+      \ target=targets[0].id)\n```\n\n`CatalogError` wraps expected failures from normalized\
+      \ discovery and option inspection. Use `describe_error()` to project any expected\
+      \ `ReadioError` into the stable `ErrorInfo` DTO for application transport. The\
+      \ module-level discovery delegates documented below remain raw compatibility APIs\
+      \ and preserve specialist results."
