+    section_hash: 4add77436c0bd72fd58b715a5c4d57bac760721a152e329affb45b6838311524
+    summary: Workflow, capability, and execution contracts
+    text: "## Workflow, capability, and execution contracts
+
+
+      `Readio.inspect(RenderRequest)` returns the canonical `WorkflowPlan`; `Readio.render(request,
+      dry_run=True)` presents that same plan. The stable JSON envelope is `readio.workflow-plan.v1`.
+      Each step provides an action, a Readio-owned `reason_code`, blockers, and logical
+      input/output artifact references. `WorkflowPlan.executable` is false if any step
+      is blocked. Human-readable reasons and `WorkflowStep.details` are diagnostic context,
+      not fields to parse for decisions. Stale or forced replacement remains blocked
+      unless the request explicitly authorizes rebuilding and the specialist reports
+      replacement as safe. Replacing an existing final output is a separate `replace_output=True`
+      authorization.
+
+
+      `describe_error()` projects expected `ReadioError` instances into `ErrorInfo`,
+      serialized as `readio.error-info.v1`. Stable codes include `invalid_request`,
+      `catalog_operation_failed`, `unsafe_workflow_state`, `workflow_replan_failed`,
+      `output_exists`, `stage_failed`, and `cancellation_requested`. Specialist codes,
+      when useful, remain nested diagnostic details and do not become Readio error codes.
+      The same `serialize_public()` layer selects versioned projections including `readio.workflow-plan.v1`,
+      `readio.render-result.v1`, `readio.error-info.v1`, `readio.capabilities.v1`, `readio.source-capabilities.v1`,
+      `readio.synthesis-capabilities.v1`, `readio.export-capabilities.v1`, and `readio.speak-result.v1`.
+      `readio.render.v3` identifies the intent format; it is separate from these response
+      schemas.
+
+
+      The read-only capability methods are `Readio.capabilities()`, `Readio.source_capabilities(path)`,
+      `Readio.synthesis_capabilities()`, and `Readio.export_capabilities()`. They normalize
+      current availability and do not create workspaces, provision dependencies, or
+      download models. `Readio.source_capabilities(path)` describes one concrete source
+      instead of claiming a global source-format catalog.
+
+
+      Pass a `CancellationToken` to `Readio.render()` or `Readio.synthesize()` for cooperative
+      cancellation at Readio-controlled boundaries and supported specialist callbacks.
+      Cancellation does not interrupt a specialist call already running. AudioExport
+      has no public mid-export cancellation callback, so Readio cannot stop an export
+      in progress. `Readio.render(request, include_report=True)` optionally returns
+      an in-memory `ExecutionReport` with stage outcomes, monotonic durations, and best-effort
+      specialist versions. Reports are not written to disk or retained as history."
