+    summary: Optional MCP adapter
+    text: "## Optional MCP adapter
+
+
+      Install the official MCP SDK extra with `python -m pip install 'readio[mcp]'`,
+      then run `python -m readio.mcp.server` under an MCP host using stdio. The server
+      exposes `speech_inspect_source`, `speech_inspect_workflow`, `speech_capabilities`,
+      `speech_list_engines`, `speech_list_voices`, `speech_render`, and `speech_speak`.
+      Tool results use the shared public serializer. Voice listing is offline and cache-only
+      by default. The render tool requires explicit source, profile, and output paths,
+      inspects before execution, and never enables rebuild or output replacement unless
+      the caller sets the corresponding controls. `speech_speak` synthesizes explicit
+      text with explicit engine and target and returns a base64 WAV payload without
+      playback. MCP remains optional and adds no hidden persistence, worker service,
+      or specialist-private API usage."
