+    section_hash: 85dad915ce666892c77aa1c482d2af915bbac130b29f4da4bc3070ab2058ef1d
+    summary: Stable contracts and fail-closed execution
+    text: "## Stable contracts and fail-closed execution
+
+
+      `Readio.inspect(RenderRequest)` is the canonical read-only planner. `status`,
+      CLI dry-run, the Python API, and MCP all present the same `WorkflowPlan`. Stable
+      reason codes, blockers, and logical artifact references describe plan state; human-readable
+      reason strings and `details` remain diagnostic only. Replacement requires explicit
+      rebuild authorization and specialist-certified safety. Existing final output replacement
+      has its own explicit control.
+
+
+      One public serializer defines the versioned JSON projections for plans, render
+      results, errors, capabilities, and synthesized speech. Intent schema `readio.render.v3`
+      is distinct from response schemas such as `readio.workflow-plan.v1`, `readio.render-result.v1`,
+      and `readio.error-info.v1`. Capability discovery is read-only. Cancellation is
+      cooperative at supported boundaries, and AudioExport cannot currently be interrupted
+      through its public API. Optional execution reports contain in-memory stage timing
+      and version metadata only."
