+    summary: Stable platform contracts and MCP
+    text: "## Stable platform contracts and MCP
+
+
+      `Readio.inspect()` is the canonical, read-only workflow plan used by `status`,
+      dry-run, and the Python API. Plans expose stable reason codes, blockers, and logical
+      artifact references; diagnostic details are not a protocol. Shared versioned serialization
+      covers plans, results, errors, capabilities, and semantic speech results. `Readio.capabilities()`
+      and scoped capability methods are read-only; cancellation is cooperative at supported
+      boundaries, and execution reports are optional and never persisted.
+
+
+      MCP is an optional adapter over `readio.api`. Install it with `python -m pip install
+      'readio[mcp]'` and launch `python -m readio.mcp.server` as a stdio server. Its
+      tools inspect sources and workflows, report capabilities, list engines and cached
+      voices, render, and synthesize speech. Rendering requires explicit source, profile,
+      and output paths. It inspects first and executes only an executable plan with
+      the request's explicit rebuild and output replacement controls. `speech_speak`
+      returns WAV audio as base64 and does not play audio. See [Python API contracts](docs/api.md)
+      and [architecture](docs/architecture.md)."
